Generally, if you get a magic lamp early enough and aren't going for the
artiwishless conduct, it is undoubtedly best to go ahead and wish for
the Quest Artifact of your choice Right Now.  Some of the QAs are
head-and-shoulders better than anything else you'll ever find, and the
opportunity to get one at 100% is just too good to pass up.

If you are maintaining artiwishless, though, then it's a little more
dicey.  In your spot, SDSM will give you a nice AC boost and a big
casting boost (since you can ditch your evil metal shield and go find
your old wooden one), which can't be bad.  But you may have to spend a
wish later on MR.  Alternately, you can go for GDSM and play a more
fighty priest for awhile.

Once I'm at a point where I can easily handle the Castle, though, I
generally always save one lamp and use the wishes from the wand there
first.  Use your own judgment on this.

> - since i haven't found any artifacts yet (it's the early game),
> wishing for an artifact will work 100%

This matters.

